 5492:                                 ; run_6ms_job
 5493:                                 ;   analysis [low]: Misaligned banner: the real routine starts at b1:A675 (bytes shown as fcb A675-A705), called
 5494:                                 ;        from bank-0 8063 via far_b1_A675_7E21. It sets TASKFLAGS1.6 (busy flag), reads the AN7 and AN2 ADCs, runs
 5495:                                 ;        Verify_spill_valve_timing, and runs the PCS force-motor PI loop and output when the config bits allow. It
 5496:                                 ;        then runs Brake_input_debounce, the TDC learn (A98C), ITS stepper (AB0C) and EGR/baro filter. E
 5497:                                 ;   inferred [C, pass A]: writes COUNTER_32HZ, TASKFLAGS1
 5498:                                 ;   OBD1 _run_6ms_job (match 0.85 p1-global): 6.25 ms job
 5499:                                 ;   this looks mostly like transmission stuff and sensor interface
